WEBVTT

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.194
Paris to the Captain.

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.294
Janeway here.

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:06.965
I've done an analysis
of our route through Botha space

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:08.973
whenever you have a minute
to check it out.

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:10.805
I'm on my way to Engineering.

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:12.175
I'll be with you
as soon as I'm done.

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:13.406
Aye, Captain.

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:14.708
Ah, Captain.

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:16.443
The computer told me
I'd find you

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:18.713
on Deck 11, Section 4B,
starboard side

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:19.844
and, sure enough, here you are.

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:21.080
What can I do for you, Neelix?

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:22.850
I assumed you'd want
to talk to me.

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:23.913
About?

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:24.924
About the Botha.

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:27.153
We're headed for their space,
and, as I've told you,

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:28.922
they're going to have
to be handled very carefully.

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:30.623
I understand, and of course
I want your counsel,

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:32.130
but, right now,
I'm late for a meeting.

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:33.996
I wouldn't put
this off too long.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.692
We're getting closer, you know.

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:36.997
Yes, I know.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.334
And I will be with you
as soon as I can.

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:46.912
Sorry I'm late.
What do you have?

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:48.106
I think we're about ready

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:49.877
to make our first attempt,
Captain.

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:51.383
If you're successful,
will the Doctor

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:53.283
be able to move freely
around the entire ship?

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:54.479
Not exactly.

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:56.489
The holo-emitters will be
set up in certain key areas...

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:57.785
the Bridge, Engineering.

00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:59.724
We'll be able to transfer
him to those locations.

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:02.250
In the same way we can now
transfer him to the holodeck?

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:03.557
Exactly.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:04.858
But if he tries
to move into an area

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:08.095
where there's no emitter field,
he'll dematerialize.

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:09.533
I have the holo-projector
on line.

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:10.536
We're ready to start.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.060
Proceed.
I don't have much time.

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:13.367
Engineering to Sick Bay.

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:14.896
Doctor, we're ready here.

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:16.374
I'm standing by.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:17.933
Okay. Here goes.

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:19.501
Initiating transfer.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:22.336
Here he comes.

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:29.144
Well, this is certainly
a brilliant feat of engineering.

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.255
What happened?

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:36.319
I'd guess the imaging interface
wasn't properly stabilized.

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:38.489
Just a small oversight.

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:39.998
No pun intended.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.897
Very amusing.

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:45.166
How long will it take you
to correct this small oversight?

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:47.264
Maybe a couple of hours.

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:49.400
Mr. Kim, I have to assess
our navigational plan

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.842
and get ready to make contact
with an alien species.

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:54.176
I can't drop everything
whenever you call.

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:56.375
Tuvok to Janeway.

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:57.474
Go ahead.

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:59.644
Captain, I would like
a half an hour of your time

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:02.780
to review the security protocols
before we encounter the Botha.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:09.091
Yes, Mr. Tuvok, somehow...
I will find half an hour.

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:10.926
Excuse me, Captain.

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:13.057
Would you come down here,
please?

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:20.639
Yes?

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:22.834
When did you last
take shore leave?

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:24.400
About two months ago.

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:26.173
Ah. How long since you've done

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:28.203
something pleasurable
for recreation?

00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:29.909
Doctor, I know
I'm a bit testy today,

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:31.075
but I can assure you...

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:33.381
How long?

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:38.387
It's... been a while.

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:40.585
I have a holonovel program.

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:42.356
It helps me unwind.

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:44.693
I haven't had time to
run it for a few weeks.

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:46.756
Well, I want you to... now.

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:48.994
Doctor, I'm really very busy.

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:51.434
I've checked
Starfleet regulations.

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:52.768
The Chief Medical Officer

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:54.329
outranks the Captain
in health matters.

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:56.706
Now, I realize
this may be the first time

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:58.938
a hologram has given an order
to a Captain,

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:03.608
but I'm ordering you to report
to the holodeck... now.

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:05.140
Aye, sir.

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:13.850
And the two of you
can get busy undoing

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:15.884
this ridiculous blunder
of yours!

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:54.426
Good afternoon, milord.

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:58.198
Will the children
be joining us for tea?

00:03:58.238 --> 00:04:00.365
Presently.

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:06.139
Lord Burleigh...

00:04:06.179 --> 00:04:07.476
is something wrong?

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:09.947
Yes.

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:11.539
Terribly wrong.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:26.328
I have fallen in love with you,
Lucie.

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:20.211
Milord.

00:06:20.246 --> 00:06:22.043
Hello, Father.

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:23.742
We're ready for tea.

00:06:23.782 --> 00:06:25.147
I want cucumber sandwiches.

00:06:25.184 --> 00:06:26.742
You'll wait your turn,
young man.

00:06:26.785 --> 00:06:28.616
What may I serve you, milord?

00:06:29.889 --> 00:06:31.447
Nothing. Thank you.

00:06:36.028 --> 00:06:37.290
I see.

00:06:40.432 --> 00:06:42.400
I want my tea in this cup,
please,

00:06:42.434 --> 00:06:44.925
and I don't want
a cucumber sandwich.

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:47.803
I don't like the way
Cook cuts them.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.138
Milord, you'll be very pleased
with the children's progress

00:06:50.175 --> 00:06:51.574
in their studies this week.

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:53.976
Henry shows a real talent
for mathematics,

00:06:54.013 --> 00:06:58.177
and Beatrice turns out to be
quite musical.

00:06:59.418 --> 00:07:01.045
Beatrice?

00:07:01.086 --> 00:07:02.713
Musical?

00:07:02.755 --> 00:07:05.246
I don't know what she means.

00:07:05.291 --> 00:07:06.553
She's very modest about it.

00:07:06.592 --> 00:07:09.584
I've heard her several times
in the music room,

00:07:09.628 --> 00:07:12.791
playing a lovely Mozart sonata,

00:07:12.831 --> 00:07:17.325
but whenever I ask her
to play it for me, she won't.

00:07:17.369 --> 00:07:19.360
I think her talent
should be encouraged.

00:07:19.405 --> 00:07:20.804
Would you consider lessons?

00:07:20.839 --> 00:07:23.399
I didn't know Beatrice
could play the piano.

00:07:27.913 --> 00:07:29.574
I'm sorry.

00:07:29.615 --> 00:07:31.742
It's just a cup.

00:07:31.784 --> 00:07:33.046
Don't be a goose.

00:07:33.085 --> 00:07:35.952
It's the flower cup...
Mother's cup.

00:07:36.055 --> 00:07:37.522
It doesn't matter!

00:07:37.556 --> 00:07:38.488
Mrs. Templeton!

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:41.516
Please take the children
to the nursery.

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:42.527
Yes, milord.

00:07:42.561 --> 00:07:43.653
Come.

00:07:46.966 --> 00:07:48.399
Please stay here,
Mrs. Davenport.

00:07:48.434 --> 00:07:49.958
Beatrice is upset.

00:07:50.069 --> 00:07:51.195
I should be with her.

00:07:51.236 --> 00:07:52.168
I want you here.

00:07:56.809 --> 00:07:58.868
What's happening in this house?

00:07:58.911 --> 00:08:02.312
How can you not know
that Beatrice plays the piano?

00:08:02.348 --> 00:08:04.509
Why shouldn't I go
to the fourth floor?

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:05.517
What's up there?

00:08:05.551 --> 00:08:07.143
Those are questions
you must not ask.

00:08:07.186 --> 00:08:08.380
But I am asking them.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:10.650
I'm worried about the children.

00:08:10.689 --> 00:08:13.283
Beatrice fantasizes that
her mother is still alive.

00:08:13.325 --> 00:08:14.792
Don't pursue this, I beg you.

00:08:14.827 --> 00:08:16.385
Bridge to the Captain.

00:08:16.428 --> 00:08:17.759
Freeze program.

00:08:20.799 --> 00:08:22.096
Janeway here.

00:08:22.134 --> 00:08:23.795
We've been hailed
by a representative

00:08:23.836 --> 00:08:25.235
of the Bothan government.

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:26.669
They'd like to talk to you.

00:08:26.705 --> 00:08:28.605
I'll be right there.

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:32.270
Sorry, milord.

00:08:32.311 --> 00:08:33.642
Duty calls.

00:08:40.019 --> 00:08:42.647
Captain, I knew we should
have talked this morning.

00:08:42.688 --> 00:08:43.882
Tell me what you know,
Neelix.

00:08:43.922 --> 00:08:47.483
I've been in subspace contact
with some old friends of mine...

00:08:47.526 --> 00:08:50.552
uh, nomads, collectors,
much as I used to be.

00:08:50.596 --> 00:08:52.530
They're in a position
to gather information

00:08:52.564 --> 00:08:53.826
during their travels.

00:08:53.866 --> 00:08:56.096
What they've told me
doesn't sound good.

00:08:56.135 --> 00:08:56.965
In what way?

00:08:57.002 --> 00:08:59.266
There are lots of rumors
about ships

00:08:59.304 --> 00:09:01.738
entering Bothan space,
never to be heard from again.

00:09:01.774 --> 00:09:03.207
My sources on Mithren say

00:09:03.242 --> 00:09:05.540
that they have lost
a number of vessels.

00:09:05.577 --> 00:09:08.273
They say the Botha protect
their territory fiercely.

00:09:08.313 --> 00:09:09.780
But we aren't aggressors.

00:09:09.815 --> 00:09:11.305
I don't think they are either.

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:14.683
They just don't want anyone
crossing their borders.

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:16.051
Will they negotiate?

00:09:16.088 --> 00:09:17.646
Will they respond to diplomacy?

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:19.282
It's hard to say.

00:09:19.324 --> 00:09:21.485
There's some belief
that they don't even have

00:09:21.527 --> 00:09:22.858
a legitimate claim
to the space...

00:09:22.895 --> 00:09:26.228
that they're nothing more
than pernicious, odious vandals,

00:09:26.265 --> 00:09:29.359
in which case, diplomacy
would fall on deaf ears.

00:09:29.401 --> 00:09:31.426
We're being hailed again,
Captain.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:32.459
On screen.

00:09:36.008 --> 00:09:37.942
I'm Kathryn Janeway

00:09:37.976 --> 00:09:40.570
of the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:09:40.612 --> 00:09:43.479
Why have you entered our space
without permission?

00:09:43.515 --> 00:09:45.745
We didn't realize
this was your space.

00:09:45.784 --> 00:09:47.251
On what basis do you claim it?

00:09:47.286 --> 00:09:50.187
I have no intention
of explaining myself to you.

00:09:50.222 --> 00:09:53.521
The fact is, you're violating
our territory.

00:09:53.559 --> 00:09:56.528
I assure you,
we mean no disrespect.

00:09:56.562 --> 00:09:58.553
We are from another part
of the galaxy.

00:09:58.597 --> 00:10:00.724
We're just trying
to make our way home.

00:10:00.766 --> 00:10:03.291
We'll send a ship
to rendezvous with you.

00:10:03.335 --> 00:10:06.736
If you meet the criteria,
we'll consider your request.

00:10:06.772 --> 00:10:08.899
Thank you.

00:10:08.941 --> 00:10:09.965
What are the criteria?

00:10:10.075 --> 00:10:12.543
We'll discuss that when we meet.

00:10:14.546 --> 00:10:16.207
Friendly fellow.

00:10:16.248 --> 00:10:18.273
At least they're willing
to talk.

00:10:18.317 --> 00:10:20.911
I wonder why he wouldn't
let us see his face.

00:10:20.953 --> 00:10:22.944
I suspect it was
a calculated move...

00:10:22.988 --> 00:10:25.115
an attempt to intimidate us.

00:10:25.157 --> 00:10:26.590
Commander, you have the Bridge.

00:10:26.625 --> 00:10:27.592
Aye, Captain.

00:10:27.626 --> 00:10:28.854
Mr. Neelix, join me
in my ready room.

00:10:28.894 --> 00:10:29.986
We should talk
about this meeting.

00:10:30.095 --> 00:10:31.562
Captain, if I may...

00:10:31.597 --> 00:10:34.122
When was the last time you ate?

00:10:34.166 --> 00:10:35.190
Ate?

00:10:35.234 --> 00:10:37.896
Oh, I had some soup last night.

00:10:37.936 --> 00:10:38.903
Then let me suggest

00:10:38.937 --> 00:10:40.529
that we conduct our
talk in the Mess Hall.

00:10:40.572 --> 00:10:43.166
We're serving a sumptuous
repast for lunch.

00:10:52.217 --> 00:10:53.411
Right.

00:10:53.452 --> 00:10:54.441
Lunch it is.

00:10:58.857 --> 00:11:02.418
Captain, you have a nasty
habit of skipping meals,

00:11:02.461 --> 00:11:04.895
and that can do horrible things
to your electrolyte levels.

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:07.194
I know, but sometimes
I just get too busy to eat.

00:11:07.232 --> 00:11:09.166
All you have to do
is give me a call.

00:11:09.201 --> 00:11:11.192
I'll be there in a trice
with a tray

00:11:11.236 --> 00:11:14.330
of foods so delectable
you won't be able to resist.

00:11:14.373 --> 00:11:18.309
I do think I've outdone
myself this time.

00:11:18.343 --> 00:11:23.975
An exquisite pâté made
from Seltin wood fungus.

00:11:24.016 --> 00:11:28.851
Brine-soaked neccel strips.

00:11:28.887 --> 00:11:29.876
Ooh.

00:11:31.824 --> 00:11:33.382
Deviled wood throk.

00:11:39.264 --> 00:11:40.822
Where did these come from?

00:11:40.866 --> 00:11:42.993
Lieutenant Hargrove
asked for them.

00:11:43.068 --> 00:11:44.501
Is something wrong?

00:11:47.172 --> 00:11:49.970
No. Just a funny coincidence.

00:11:50.008 --> 00:11:51.873
Something I saw on the holodeck.

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:54.936
Thank you, Neelix.

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:56.208
This all looks delicious.

00:11:56.248 --> 00:11:58.341
And it's bound to boost
my electrolyte levels.

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:03.851
Where did you get that cup?

00:12:03.889 --> 00:12:05.447
Why, I'm not sure.

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:07.788
I think I found several
of them in storage.

00:12:09.361 --> 00:12:11.192
Unusual, isn't it?

00:12:12.798 --> 00:12:16.700
Captain,
is everything all right?

00:12:19.104 --> 00:12:20.469
It's perfectly all right,
Neelix.

00:12:23.609 --> 00:12:27.739
I just have to remind myself
that coincidences do happen.

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:37.318
I can't help myself.

00:12:37.356 --> 00:12:39.256
I've fallen in love with you.

00:13:05.817 --> 00:13:06.875
My mother is alive

00:13:06.919 --> 00:13:10.480
and my father loves her,
not you.

00:13:20.499 --> 00:13:22.399
In the course of your
experiments with the Doctor,

00:13:22.434 --> 00:13:24.368
have you accessed
any of the holodeck programs?

00:13:24.403 --> 00:13:26.098
No, we're bypassing
the holodecks.

00:13:26.138 --> 00:13:27.730
Where did you get
this holo-projector?

00:13:27.773 --> 00:13:29.070
We found several of them
in storage.

00:13:29.107 --> 00:13:31.268
We've been reconfiguring
them one by one.

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:32.971
So you haven't worked directly
with any of the projectors

00:13:33.078 --> 00:13:34.409
on the holodecks?

00:13:34.446 --> 00:13:35.606
No.

00:13:35.647 --> 00:13:37.979
Is there anything you've done...

00:13:38.016 --> 00:13:39.847
anything you can think of...
that might have caused

00:13:39.885 --> 00:13:41.546
holographic objects
and characters

00:13:41.586 --> 00:13:43.520
to appear outside the holodeck?

00:13:43.555 --> 00:13:45.523
Not that I'm aware of.

00:13:46.558 --> 00:13:50.085
I was sure your experiments
would explain it.

00:13:51.196 --> 00:13:54.165
Captain,
there has to be a reason

00:13:54.199 --> 00:13:55.791
why you've had these delusions.

00:13:55.834 --> 00:13:57.267
And we're going to figure
out what it is.

00:13:57.302 --> 00:14:00.669
The Doctor pointed out that
I've been under some stress.

00:14:00.706 --> 00:14:02.697
I can't ignore that.

00:14:02.741 --> 00:14:03.730
I think we should check out

00:14:03.775 --> 00:14:05.436
the imaging systems
on the holodeck.

00:14:05.477 --> 00:14:07.809
There might be
a simple malfunction.

00:14:07.846 --> 00:14:08.904
Good idea.

00:14:08.947 --> 00:14:10.938
We can run the diagnostic
from here in Engineering,

00:14:10.983 --> 00:14:12.644
but you should activate
the program first.

00:14:12.684 --> 00:14:14.515
I'll contact you
from the holodeck.

00:14:24.229 --> 00:14:25.457
Janeway to Engineering.

00:14:25.497 --> 00:14:26.464
Torres here.

00:14:26.498 --> 00:14:27.965
Have you set up the diagnostic?

00:14:28.066 --> 00:14:29.192
We're ready, Captain.

00:14:31.236 --> 00:14:32.828
Go ahead.

00:14:32.871 --> 00:14:34.361
Lucie!

00:14:34.406 --> 00:14:36.567
Thank God you've come back.

00:14:39.511 --> 00:14:41.638
Why are you dressed
so strangely?

00:14:43.382 --> 00:14:45.247
It's...

00:14:45.283 --> 00:14:46.545
a costume.

00:14:46.585 --> 00:14:49.179
You'd look lovely in anything.

00:14:49.221 --> 00:14:52.782
I've thought of you constantly.

00:14:52.824 --> 00:14:55.292
Remembered your touch...

00:14:55.327 --> 00:14:56.851
your perfume...

00:14:56.895 --> 00:14:58.920
your lips.

00:15:00.465 --> 00:15:02.399
Computer, delete character.

00:15:02.434 --> 00:15:04.493
Torres to Janeway.

00:15:04.536 --> 00:15:05.503
We're finished, Captain,

00:15:05.537 --> 00:15:06.834
but we didn't find
any malfunctions.

00:15:06.872 --> 00:15:09.397
Recalibrate and try it again.

00:15:09.441 --> 00:15:11.932
I'm going to check
something else.

00:15:12.044 --> 00:15:13.443
Aye, Captain.

00:15:16.882 --> 00:15:17.906
Captain!

00:15:17.949 --> 00:15:19.940
I'm delighted to see you.

00:15:19.985 --> 00:15:21.384
Do you want a snack?

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:22.512
No, I'm fine.

00:15:22.554 --> 00:15:24.613
But I wanted to ask you
about lunch.

00:15:24.656 --> 00:15:27.284
Didn't you like it?

00:15:27.325 --> 00:15:28.690
It was delicious.

00:15:28.727 --> 00:15:30.922
I was just trying to remember
all the dishes you made.

00:15:30.962 --> 00:15:32.930
There was... the Seltin pâté.

00:15:32.964 --> 00:15:34.192
Delectable.

00:15:34.232 --> 00:15:35.324
The neccel strips.

00:15:35.367 --> 00:15:36.425
Exquisite.

00:15:36.468 --> 00:15:37.730
The deviled throk.

00:15:37.769 --> 00:15:39.168
Sublime.

00:15:39.204 --> 00:15:41.172
And the cucumber sandwiches.

00:15:41.206 --> 00:15:43.436
Cucumber sandwiches?

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:46.575
Weren't there...

00:15:46.611 --> 00:15:48.078
cucumber sandwiches?

00:15:48.113 --> 00:15:50.308
I don't even know what that is.

00:15:50.348 --> 00:15:53.340
The other item on the menu
was a fried murt cake.

00:15:53.385 --> 00:15:54.443
You ate one.

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:57.654
And the cup you served
my tea in?

00:16:00.592 --> 00:16:02.150
One of these.

00:16:03.628 --> 00:16:05.061
The ones I found in storage.

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:09.697
I thought...

00:16:11.103 --> 00:16:12.604
it had flowers on it.

00:16:12.737 --> 00:16:14.261
Flowers?

00:16:14.305 --> 00:16:17.274
Well, no,
I don't see any flowers.

00:16:17.308 --> 00:16:19.173
Maybe there was another cup,

00:16:19.210 --> 00:16:20.939
but I-I don't think so.

00:16:22.313 --> 00:16:24.508
Would you like a cup
with flowers on it?

00:16:24.549 --> 00:16:26.244
I'm sure I could replicate one.

00:16:26.284 --> 00:16:28.184
It's all right, Neelix.

00:16:28.219 --> 00:16:30.551
You've told me
what I need to know.

00:16:36.828 --> 00:16:38.728
I don't detect anything so far.

00:16:38.763 --> 00:16:41.197
No evidence of aneurysm...

00:16:41.232 --> 00:16:43.598
subdural hematoma...

00:16:43.635 --> 00:16:44.966
stroke.

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:49.068
Could it be... stress?

00:16:49.107 --> 00:16:50.233
Possibly.

00:16:50.274 --> 00:16:52.333
Did you go to the holodeck,
as I ordered?

00:16:52.377 --> 00:16:53.344
Yes.

00:16:53.378 --> 00:16:54.902
And was that relaxing?

00:16:57.248 --> 00:16:58.681
It was interesting.

00:16:58.716 --> 00:17:01.150
I'm not sure
how relaxing it was.

00:17:01.185 --> 00:17:04.177
There are other possibilities
we should consider.

00:17:04.222 --> 00:17:08.556
I want to scan for airborne
bacteria and viruses.

00:17:08.593 --> 00:17:10.288
We should investigate
the possibility

00:17:10.328 --> 00:17:11.920
of an alien intruder.

00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:15.522
And I'd like to do
a cerebro-cortical scan on you.

00:17:15.566 --> 00:17:17.557
Oh!

00:17:17.602 --> 00:17:19.331
Kes?

00:17:19.370 --> 00:17:22.567
I... I don't know.

00:17:22.607 --> 00:17:24.541
Strange.

00:17:25.677 --> 00:17:28.441
Suddenly, I felt cold, shivery.

00:17:28.479 --> 00:17:30.879
Someone was walking
on your grave.

00:17:30.915 --> 00:17:31.882
Hmm?

00:17:34.218 --> 00:17:36.083
Just an old saying on Earth.

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:39.783
A way of describing
an odd feeling like that.

00:17:39.824 --> 00:17:41.348
Hmm. How macabre.

00:17:41.392 --> 00:17:42.620
It's a human expression,
Doctor.

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:44.184
I'd think you'd have heard it.

00:17:44.228 --> 00:17:45.889
My programmers
didn't clutter me up

00:17:45.930 --> 00:17:47.522
with pithy Earth trivia.

00:17:47.565 --> 00:17:50.534
They programmed me
with far more important data.

00:17:50.568 --> 00:17:53.332
Kes, would you please get

00:17:53.371 --> 00:17:54.565
my sub-neural scanner
from the med lab?

00:17:54.605 --> 00:17:55.799
Yes, Doctor.

00:17:58.242 --> 00:18:00.107
What about my mother's grave?

00:18:00.144 --> 00:18:02.271
There's no one inside.

00:18:02.313 --> 00:18:04.213
The coffin is empty.

00:18:04.248 --> 00:18:06.341
Doctor. Doctor.

00:18:08.853 --> 00:18:10.821
Who do you see here?

00:18:13.591 --> 00:18:14.785
I see you.

00:18:14.826 --> 00:18:17.192
And I see you...

00:18:17.228 --> 00:18:21.221
but I also see a little girl
from my holodeck program.

00:18:33.544 --> 00:18:35.171
What happened?

00:18:39.383 --> 00:18:41.578
I'm not sure.

00:18:41.619 --> 00:18:44.884
The image of the little girl
suddenly rushed at me.

00:18:44.922 --> 00:18:46.913
I saw it, too.

00:18:46.958 --> 00:18:50.121
When I came in...

00:18:50.161 --> 00:18:51.719
I felt as though
something hit me...

00:18:51.763 --> 00:18:52.821
bounced off me...

00:18:52.864 --> 00:18:55.424
then I saw the little girl
moving right into you.

00:18:57.201 --> 00:18:59.101
As though you became a mirror.

00:18:59.137 --> 00:19:02.197
You reflected her back
toward me.

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:05.038
I've been doing some
mental exercises with Tuvok

00:19:05.076 --> 00:19:06.634
developing
my telepathic abilities,

00:19:06.677 --> 00:19:08.975
but we haven't done
anything like this.

00:19:10.782 --> 00:19:13.774
Captain, until I am able
to determine

00:19:13.818 --> 00:19:15.080
the cause
of these hallucinations,

00:19:15.119 --> 00:19:16.916
I'd prefer that you return
to your quarters.

00:19:17.021 --> 00:19:18.420
Get some rest.

00:19:30.868 --> 00:19:32.597
Vegetable bouillon.

00:19:33.604 --> 00:19:34.935
No, cancel that.

00:19:34.972 --> 00:19:36.963
Coffee ice cream.

00:20:02.900 --> 00:20:04.060
Hello?

00:20:12.643 --> 00:20:13.610
Is anyone there?

00:20:16.280 --> 00:20:18.271
Computer...

00:20:18.316 --> 00:20:21.251
is there anyone
in these quarters except me?

00:20:21.285 --> 00:20:23.219
Negative.

00:20:31.462 --> 00:20:34.090
Kath, are you there?

00:20:34.131 --> 00:20:35.962
Who's that?

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.490
Come look at the puppies.

00:20:37.535 --> 00:20:39.093
Mark...

00:21:32.490 --> 00:21:35.118
I've missed you so much, Kath.

00:21:35.159 --> 00:21:37.150
When are you coming back?

00:21:37.194 --> 00:21:40.425
I don't think you've missed me.

00:21:40.464 --> 00:21:44.093
Someone else
is in your thoughts now.

00:21:51.008 --> 00:21:52.703
Isn't that true?

00:21:52.743 --> 00:21:54.233
Isn't there someone
you're thinking of?

00:21:54.278 --> 00:21:56.075
Computer, open the door.

00:21:57.548 --> 00:22:01.245
Everything was fine
until you came here.

00:22:02.687 --> 00:22:04.450
I took care of him.

00:22:04.488 --> 00:22:06.251
He trusted me,

00:22:06.290 --> 00:22:09.953
but when you arrived,
all that changed.

00:22:10.027 --> 00:22:10.959
Janeway to Security.

00:22:11.028 --> 00:22:12.086
Intruder alert.

00:22:12.129 --> 00:22:14.825
You've done nothing
but cause trouble.

00:22:14.865 --> 00:22:18.130
We don't want
more trouble in our lives!

00:22:23.441 --> 00:22:25.272
Security
to the Captain's quarters!

00:22:25.309 --> 00:22:26.970
Tuvok, please respond!

00:22:27.011 --> 00:22:27.978
Captain!

00:22:28.012 --> 00:22:28.979
Can you still see
the hallucination?

00:22:29.046 --> 00:22:30.308
Yes. The woman with the knife

00:22:30.348 --> 00:22:32.179
is receding into the Captain
just like before.

00:22:32.216 --> 00:22:33.581
Captain, listen to me!

00:22:33.617 --> 00:22:35.346
You are in Sick Bay.

00:22:35.386 --> 00:22:37.320
You are all right.

00:22:37.355 --> 00:22:38.913
Captain!

00:22:57.441 --> 00:22:58.408
I think Neelix can help you.

00:22:58.442 --> 00:22:59.568
No one knows much
about the Botha,

00:22:59.610 --> 00:23:00.542
but he has some information.

00:23:00.578 --> 00:23:01.670
I know he's been doing research.

00:23:01.712 --> 00:23:02.679
I'll check with him.

00:23:02.713 --> 00:23:04.305
You'll probably want him
on the Bridge with you

00:23:04.348 --> 00:23:05.315
when their ship arrives.

00:23:05.349 --> 00:23:06.316
Good idea.

00:23:06.350 --> 00:23:07.749
I'm not sure how Torres
and Kim are coming.

00:23:07.785 --> 00:23:08.945
You know they're
trying to find a way

00:23:09.053 --> 00:23:10.350
to transfer the Doctor
out of Sick Bay.

00:23:10.388 --> 00:23:11.355
Yes.

00:23:11.389 --> 00:23:12.356
It's not a priority,

00:23:12.390 --> 00:23:13.755
but you might want
to stay on top of it.

00:23:13.791 --> 00:23:14.917
Of course.
Let's see.

00:23:14.959 --> 00:23:16.756
There was a problem with one
of the deflector shields.

00:23:16.794 --> 00:23:17.886
You'll want
to follow up on that.

00:23:17.928 --> 00:23:18.895
And Stellar Cartography

00:23:18.929 --> 00:23:21.124
was hoping for a review
of their latest report.

00:23:21.165 --> 00:23:22.359
I think Tuvok wanted to discuss

00:23:22.400 --> 00:23:23.765
something
about weapons storage...

00:23:23.801 --> 00:23:25.200
Captain.

00:23:25.236 --> 00:23:27.363
You've trained your crew well.

00:23:27.405 --> 00:23:29.600
We'll be able to do without you
for a few days.

00:23:29.640 --> 00:23:30.538
In the meantime,

00:23:30.574 --> 00:23:33.600
we're continuing diagnostics
on all ship's systems.

00:23:33.644 --> 00:23:35.669
There's a reason
for what's happening to you

00:23:35.713 --> 00:23:37.146
and we're not stopping
until we find it.

00:23:37.181 --> 00:23:38.170
Thank you, Commander.

00:23:38.215 --> 00:23:39.546
My patient has to rest now.

00:23:39.583 --> 00:23:41.676
I'm sure you'll want
to get to the Bridge.

00:23:41.719 --> 00:23:43.516
Call me if there's
anything I can do.

00:23:43.554 --> 00:23:45.579
Just be sure to report to me
after you meet with the Botha.

00:23:45.623 --> 00:23:46.590
Yes, ma'am.

00:23:46.624 --> 00:23:47.818
Captain, if you'll take a seat
on one of the beds,

00:23:47.858 --> 00:23:49.849
I'd like to do
some further tests.

00:23:49.894 --> 00:23:50.622
Kes, please
prepare the Captain

00:23:50.661 --> 00:23:52.390
for a cerebro-cortical scan.

00:23:52.430 --> 00:23:53.829
Certainly.

00:23:53.864 --> 00:23:56.594
Captain, I saw
your hallucination again.

00:23:56.634 --> 00:23:57.999
What did you see?

00:23:58.035 --> 00:23:59.400
You were struggling
with a woman.

00:23:59.437 --> 00:24:00.461
She had a knife.

00:24:00.504 --> 00:24:02.404
She was trying to hurt you.

00:24:02.440 --> 00:24:03.930
- That's right.
- As I focused on you,

00:24:04.041 --> 00:24:05.872
it was just like
with the little girl...

00:24:05.910 --> 00:24:07.707
the image seemed
to reflect off of me

00:24:07.745 --> 00:24:09.110
and move back into you.

00:24:09.146 --> 00:24:11.774
Your telepathic abilities
must be increasing.

00:24:11.816 --> 00:24:13.374
I think it's more than that.

00:24:13.417 --> 00:24:15.783
I think something strange
is happening on this ship,

00:24:15.820 --> 00:24:17.811
and it's not
just happening to you.

00:24:19.824 --> 00:24:21.587
I am picking up a ship

00:24:21.625 --> 00:24:22.785
on long-range sensors,
Commander.

00:24:22.827 --> 00:24:25.853
It is a design
we have not encountered before.

00:24:25.896 --> 00:24:27.955
I show it
on a direct intercept course.

00:24:28.032 --> 00:24:29.499
That must be
our welcoming party.

00:24:29.533 --> 00:24:30.966
They're in a hurry, too.

00:24:31.035 --> 00:24:32.059
Closing fast.

00:24:32.103 --> 00:24:33.331
They are hailing, Commander.

00:24:33.370 --> 00:24:34.701
On screen.

00:24:34.738 --> 00:24:37.138
Where is your Captain?

00:24:37.174 --> 00:24:38.937
She's not available right now.

00:24:38.976 --> 00:24:41.240
I'm Commander Chakotay,
the First Officer.

00:24:41.278 --> 00:24:42.506
I can speak for her.

00:24:42.546 --> 00:24:44.275
We observe
rather strict protocols.

00:24:44.315 --> 00:24:47.842
I'd prefer to negotiate
with the Captain.

00:24:47.885 --> 00:24:50.353
I understand, but she's not able
to come to the Bridge now,

00:24:50.387 --> 00:24:52.582
and in her absence,
our protocols allow me

00:24:52.623 --> 00:24:53.988
to assume her place.

00:24:54.058 --> 00:24:55.491
Our request is the same.

00:24:55.526 --> 00:24:57.892
We'd like permission
to cross through your space.

00:24:57.928 --> 00:24:59.327
We'll do it
as quickly as possible.

00:24:59.363 --> 00:25:02.196
What kind of weapon systems
do you possess?

00:25:03.400 --> 00:25:05.595
I'm not sure why that
information is necessary.

00:25:05.636 --> 00:25:08.196
How do I know you aren't
a heavily armed invader,

00:25:08.239 --> 00:25:09.900
here to attack our settlements?

00:25:09.940 --> 00:25:12.170
I don't know
how to convince you,

00:25:12.209 --> 00:25:13.176
but we're a peaceful people.

00:25:13.210 --> 00:25:15.644
If you doubt us...

00:25:15.679 --> 00:25:16.475
What happened?

00:25:16.514 --> 00:25:18.709
I terminated
the transmission, Commander,

00:25:18.749 --> 00:25:20.944
and made it look like
an accidental interruption.

00:25:21.051 --> 00:25:23.713
I am concerned about
some anomalous sensor readings.

00:25:23.754 --> 00:25:24.948
I'm getting them, too.

00:25:25.055 --> 00:25:26.818
Residual energy displacements.

00:25:26.857 --> 00:25:28.381
Two discrete readings...

00:25:28.425 --> 00:25:30.120
one off the port bow,
one off starboard.

00:25:30.161 --> 00:25:32.789
We have to consider the
possibility of cloaked ships.

00:25:32.830 --> 00:25:34.695
Reverse course, Mr. Paris.

00:25:34.732 --> 00:25:35.699
Aye, sir.

00:25:36.834 --> 00:25:38.165
Two ships de-cloaking.

00:25:40.037 --> 00:25:42.562
The Bothan ship
is powering up weapons.

00:25:42.606 --> 00:25:44.267
Evasive maneuver gamma five.

00:25:47.378 --> 00:25:48.345
Report.

00:25:48.379 --> 00:25:49.971
Shields at 87 percent.

00:25:50.080 --> 00:25:51.980
Minor damage on Decks 4 and 12.

00:25:52.016 --> 00:25:53.643
They're turning back
for another strike.

00:25:53.684 --> 00:25:55.743
Initiating
evasive pattern beta two.

00:25:55.786 --> 00:25:56.912
Get the weapons on line.

00:25:56.954 --> 00:25:58.979
Powering up
lateral phaser arrays.

00:25:59.957 --> 00:26:02.050
Shields down to 83 percent.

00:26:02.092 --> 00:26:04.494
Return fire.

00:26:07.463 --> 00:26:09.090
A direct hit.

00:26:09.131 --> 00:26:10.962
However, their shields
were not penetrated.

00:26:14.237 --> 00:26:15.465
I can't stay here.

00:26:15.505 --> 00:26:17.803
Captain, I can't allow
you to leave Sick Bay.

00:26:17.840 --> 00:26:19.467
- You're in no condition...
- Sorry, Doctor.

00:26:19.509 --> 00:26:21.534
If we're in trouble,
my place is on the Bridge.

00:26:23.779 --> 00:26:25.542
There's something weird
going on, Commander.

00:26:25.581 --> 00:26:26.843
I'm not reading any life signs

00:26:26.883 --> 00:26:28.350
on the two ships
that just de-cloaked.

00:26:28.384 --> 00:26:29.351
There's no crew?

00:26:29.385 --> 00:26:31.353
It looks like the ships
are automated.

00:26:31.387 --> 00:26:33.719
They're being controlled
by the Bothan ship.

00:26:35.024 --> 00:26:36.616
Return fire, Tuvok.

00:26:39.695 --> 00:26:41.094
We have hit their weapons array,

00:26:41.130 --> 00:26:43.121
but not severely enough
to disable it.

00:26:43.165 --> 00:26:45.929
Commander, the three ships
are maneuvering to surround us.

00:26:45.968 --> 00:26:47.959
Get us out of here, Paris.

00:26:48.070 --> 00:26:49.901
I'm trying.

00:26:49.939 --> 00:26:51.304
The ships are powering
their weapons.

00:26:51.340 --> 00:26:52.932
Preparing to fire.

00:26:57.613 --> 00:27:00.411
That last volley took
our shields down to 21 percent.

00:27:00.449 --> 00:27:01.780
We've got damage on all decks.

00:27:01.817 --> 00:27:02.784
Reports of injuries.

00:27:04.186 --> 00:27:06.211
All stop.

00:27:11.928 --> 00:27:13.896
The lead ship is hailing us,
Commander.

00:27:13.930 --> 00:27:15.420
On screen.

00:27:15.464 --> 00:27:19.730
Your ship is damaged
and your Captain incapacitated.

00:27:19.769 --> 00:27:22.465
I will accept
your immediate surrender.

00:27:22.505 --> 00:27:24.097
You're not getting one.

00:27:24.140 --> 00:27:25.732
The Captain is fine.

00:27:25.775 --> 00:27:26.764
I don't think so.

00:27:26.809 --> 00:27:30.472
I think the battle is over now.

00:27:38.421 --> 00:27:39.410
Mark.

00:27:42.091 --> 00:27:45.219
Don't you recognize
the man you love?

00:27:51.400 --> 00:27:54.995
Mr. Paris, who do you see
on the viewscreen?

00:27:56.572 --> 00:28:00.372
It's... my father.

00:28:00.409 --> 00:28:03.071
I hope you've been
behaving yourself.

00:28:04.947 --> 00:28:06.574
I see my girlfriend, Libby.

00:28:06.616 --> 00:28:08.914
Mr. Kim, shut down visual.

00:28:10.720 --> 00:28:12.085
I'm trying, Captain.

00:28:12.121 --> 00:28:13.349
It won't terminate.

00:28:13.389 --> 00:28:16.222
Mr. Tuvok, do a multiphasic
scan on those ships.

00:28:16.258 --> 00:28:18.249
I want any evidence
of defensive weakness

00:28:18.294 --> 00:28:21.695
and prepare the forward
photon torpedoes for launch.

00:28:21.731 --> 00:28:23.722
Tuvok?

00:28:23.766 --> 00:28:27.293
I do not understand
how this can be.

00:28:27.336 --> 00:28:29.930
Don't try to understand, Tuvok.

00:28:29.972 --> 00:28:31.496
Just accept it.

00:28:31.540 --> 00:28:33.337
We're together again.

00:28:33.376 --> 00:28:34.934
No.

00:28:35.011 --> 00:28:36.842
You are not my wife.

00:28:36.879 --> 00:28:40.474
Of course I am.
I'm T'Pel.

00:28:40.516 --> 00:28:44.543
And there, right
in front of you, is your lute,

00:28:44.587 --> 00:28:47.613
the one you used to play for me.

00:28:50.292 --> 00:28:54.058
And look... look around you.

00:28:54.096 --> 00:28:57.554
You're back home on Vulcan.

00:29:00.970 --> 00:29:02.028
Tuvok?

00:29:02.071 --> 00:29:04.164
Tuvok, answer me.

00:29:04.206 --> 00:29:06.197
Tuvok!

00:29:06.242 --> 00:29:07.504
Captain, I'll do it.

00:29:07.543 --> 00:29:08.805
Running a multiphasic scan.

00:29:08.844 --> 00:29:10.812
Torres to the Captain.

00:29:10.846 --> 00:29:11.574
Janeway here.

00:29:11.614 --> 00:29:13.138
We're having problems down here.

00:29:13.182 --> 00:29:14.581
People are becoming delusional.

00:29:14.617 --> 00:29:15.914
It's happening here, too.

00:29:15.951 --> 00:29:17.816
I think I know why.

00:29:17.853 --> 00:29:20.481
There's a massive energy field
coming from those ships.

00:29:20.523 --> 00:29:23.924
It's bioelectric, modulating
on a delta-wave frequency.

00:29:24.026 --> 00:29:27.792
It has psionic properties,
and it's permeating the hull.

00:29:27.830 --> 00:29:30.094
A psionic field
has a psychoactive effect.

00:29:30.132 --> 00:29:31.690
That would explain
the hallucinations.

00:29:31.734 --> 00:29:33.065
You can try remodulating

00:29:33.102 --> 00:29:34.933
the shields,
but, in the meantime,

00:29:35.004 --> 00:29:37.871
I'm going to set up a resonance
burst from the warp core.

00:29:37.907 --> 00:29:39.397
That'll probably
block the field,

00:29:39.442 --> 00:29:40.932
but it'll take
a while to set up.

00:29:41.010 --> 00:29:42.272
Notify the Doctor.

00:29:42.311 --> 00:29:43.710
If the field is bioelectric,

00:29:43.746 --> 00:29:45.646
he might have some ideas
how to neutralize it.

00:29:45.681 --> 00:29:47.649
Commander, give Lieutenant
Torres a hand in Engineering.

00:29:47.683 --> 00:29:49.514
Mr. Neelix, if the crew

00:29:49.552 --> 00:29:51.486
ever needed a morale officer,
now is the time.

00:29:51.520 --> 00:29:52.384
See if you can help.

00:29:52.421 --> 00:29:53.410
Aye, Captain.

00:29:53.456 --> 00:29:56.550
Kath, do you always
have to be the Captain?

00:29:56.592 --> 00:29:59.083
Can't you relax for a minute?

00:29:59.128 --> 00:30:00.390
I want to talk to you.

00:30:00.429 --> 00:30:03.728
Mr. Kim, remodulate the shields
on a rotating frequency.

00:30:08.871 --> 00:30:10.236
Janeway to Kes.

00:30:10.272 --> 00:30:11.239
Yes, Captain?

00:30:11.273 --> 00:30:12.331
Can you come to the Bridge?

00:30:12.374 --> 00:30:13.398
I think we could use you.

00:30:13.442 --> 00:30:14.409
Right away.

00:30:14.443 --> 00:30:16.206
Paris, are you still with me?

00:30:16.245 --> 00:30:17.371
Sure am, Captain.

00:30:17.413 --> 00:30:19.313
I'm running the scans
on those ships.

00:30:19.348 --> 00:30:20.315
I'll work on the shields.

00:30:20.349 --> 00:30:21.976
I suggest you don't look
at the viewscreen.

00:30:22.051 --> 00:30:24.315
It's not even tempting.

00:30:28.424 --> 00:30:29.550
How's it going down here?

00:30:29.592 --> 00:30:30.490
Not good.

00:30:30.526 --> 00:30:32.494
I can't get a response
from anybody.

00:30:32.528 --> 00:30:33.927
It's like they're catatonic.

00:30:33.963 --> 00:30:35.521
It's the same all over the ship.

00:30:35.564 --> 00:30:37.361
On my way here,
I must have seen 50 people

00:30:37.399 --> 00:30:38.764
just sitting, staring.

00:30:38.801 --> 00:30:40.826
A few minutes ago, there was
a momentary interruption

00:30:40.870 --> 00:30:42.235
in the psionic field.

00:30:42.271 --> 00:30:43.738
Were there any indications

00:30:43.773 --> 00:30:45.832
that the alien
somehow came on board?

00:30:45.875 --> 00:30:47.001
I'll find out.

00:30:47.042 --> 00:30:49.272
Chakotay to Janeway.

00:30:50.679 --> 00:30:54.012
Chakotay to the Captain.
Please respond.

00:30:55.651 --> 00:30:57.585
Chakotay to anyone
on the Bridge.

00:30:57.620 --> 00:30:59.315
Kim, Paris, anybody!

00:30:59.355 --> 00:31:02.620
We may be the last ones left.

00:31:02.658 --> 00:31:04.285
What do we do?

00:31:04.326 --> 00:31:07.523
I think we should take
an escape pod.

00:31:07.563 --> 00:31:10.088
We passed an M-Class planet
yesterday.

00:31:10.132 --> 00:31:11.497
The pod should get us there
in a week.

00:31:11.534 --> 00:31:12.762
We can try to get help.

00:31:12.802 --> 00:31:14.565
A week?
That might be too late.

00:31:14.603 --> 00:31:15.570
It may be our only hope.

00:31:15.604 --> 00:31:17.970
If we stay here,
we'll end up like the others.

00:31:18.073 --> 00:31:20.268
No. I have to keep trying
to set up the resonance burst.

00:31:20.309 --> 00:31:21.241
Do I have to give you an order?

00:31:21.277 --> 00:31:22.972
I can't believe
you're saying this.

00:31:23.078 --> 00:31:24.978
You know we have to stay here
and try to help the others.

00:31:25.080 --> 00:31:26.980
I want you with me.

00:31:27.082 --> 00:31:29.744
You aren't Chakotay.

00:31:29.785 --> 00:31:33.243
I'm the Chakotay
you want me to be.

00:31:33.289 --> 00:31:35.849
The one who loves you.

00:31:35.891 --> 00:31:38.758
This is what you want, isn't it?

00:31:38.794 --> 00:31:41.160
The secret you've been keeping?

00:31:41.197 --> 00:31:43.665
You want us to be together.

00:31:54.743 --> 00:31:56.370
And we can be.

00:32:02.518 --> 00:32:03.951
I have to help the others.

00:32:03.986 --> 00:32:05.715
I want you.

00:32:05.754 --> 00:32:07.517
I've always wanted you.

00:32:08.457 --> 00:32:10.789
You feel the same way, too.

00:32:12.962 --> 00:32:14.020
Yes!

00:32:19.034 --> 00:32:22.936
Captain, I'm getting results
from the scans.

00:32:22.972 --> 00:32:25.202
No apparent
defensive weaknesses.

00:32:25.241 --> 00:32:27.266
Metallurgical analysis
is inconclusive.

00:32:27.309 --> 00:32:28.571
I can't remodulate
the shields.

00:32:28.611 --> 00:32:29.771
Try moving us out of here.

00:32:29.812 --> 00:32:31.643
If we can get some distance
between us and those ships,

00:32:31.680 --> 00:32:32.942
we might be able
to block the effects.

00:32:32.982 --> 00:32:34.916
Yes, ma'am.

00:32:34.950 --> 00:32:37.111
This time,
let's see if you can do it

00:32:37.152 --> 00:32:38.779
without causing an accident.

00:32:38.821 --> 00:32:41.346
You usually manage
to make a mess

00:32:41.390 --> 00:32:42.721
of everything you do.

00:32:45.828 --> 00:32:49.662
Let me say something
I've always wanted to say.

00:32:49.698 --> 00:32:53.395
Get out of my life!

00:32:53.435 --> 00:32:55.699
I'm just telling you
what you already know.

00:32:55.738 --> 00:32:58.798
When the going gets tough,
you crumble.

00:32:58.841 --> 00:33:00.775
Not anymore.

00:33:02.311 --> 00:33:04.438
Not anymore.

00:33:04.480 --> 00:33:07.643
You don't really believe that
in your heart.

00:33:07.683 --> 00:33:11.551
You believe you'll fail again
and, of course, you will.

00:33:13.422 --> 00:33:15.117
You can't do anything right.

00:33:15.157 --> 00:33:16.146
You'll fail.

00:33:17.192 --> 00:33:18.750
Why even try?

00:33:22.197 --> 00:33:23.391
Tom?

00:33:26.435 --> 00:33:28.562
Tom?

00:33:28.604 --> 00:33:30.538
Janeway to Engineering.

00:33:30.572 --> 00:33:32.369
Janeway to Torres.
Are you there?

00:33:32.408 --> 00:33:34.376
Engineering, respond.

00:33:34.410 --> 00:33:36.469
If anyone in Engineering
can hear me, I'm on my way.

00:33:36.512 --> 00:33:38.946
Computer, put the Bridge
controls on security lockout.

00:33:47.022 --> 00:33:48.455
Deck 11.

00:33:51.226 --> 00:33:54.320
Now maybe you have
time to talk to me.

00:33:54.363 --> 00:33:57.230
You're so strong, Kath.

00:33:57.266 --> 00:34:00.429
It's one of the things
I always loved in you.

00:34:05.541 --> 00:34:07.099
What's the matter?

00:34:07.142 --> 00:34:08.700
You used to love it
when I kissed you there.

00:34:08.744 --> 00:34:11.508
I don't know who you are...
what you are...

00:34:11.547 --> 00:34:13.242
but I won't let you touch me.

00:34:13.282 --> 00:34:15.045
What about the man
on the holodeck?

00:34:15.084 --> 00:34:18.053
You didn't seem to mind
him touching you, did you?

00:34:18.087 --> 00:34:20.453
In fact, I think you liked it.

00:34:20.489 --> 00:34:23.754
Now I ask you, Kath,
is that fair to me?

00:34:23.792 --> 00:34:25.157
I've stayed faithful to you.

00:34:25.194 --> 00:34:27.958
I've vowed to wait for you
no matter how long it takes.

00:34:28.063 --> 00:34:30.827
Shouldn't you do the same?

00:34:41.844 --> 00:34:45.439
I haven't been unfaithful.

00:34:45.481 --> 00:34:47.312
Oh, Kath...

00:35:01.296 --> 00:35:02.729
Sick Bay to Engineering.

00:35:03.732 --> 00:35:05.563
Lieutenant Torres,
please respond.

00:35:07.269 --> 00:35:08.634
Doctor to the Mess Hall.

00:35:08.670 --> 00:35:10.194
Mr. Neelix, are you there?

00:35:11.206 --> 00:35:13.834
This is the Doctor
to anyone on the ship.

00:35:13.876 --> 00:35:16.106
If you can hear me,
please reply.

00:35:18.547 --> 00:35:20.947
Either the communications system
is malfunctioning

00:35:21.016 --> 00:35:22.347
or everyone on board

00:35:22.384 --> 00:35:24.648
has succumbed
to a delusional state.

00:35:24.686 --> 00:35:26.153
Except you and me.

00:35:26.188 --> 00:35:27.246
It would appear that,

00:35:27.289 --> 00:35:28.950
if the psionic field
is to be blocked

00:35:28.991 --> 00:35:30.424
and the crew restored to normal,

00:35:30.459 --> 00:35:31.949
it's up to us.

00:35:32.027 --> 00:35:34.655
You will have to go
to Engineering

00:35:34.696 --> 00:35:36.391
and complete
Lieutenant Torres' efforts

00:35:36.432 --> 00:35:37.831
to create a resonance burst.

00:35:37.866 --> 00:35:39.561
I don't know how to do that.

00:35:39.601 --> 00:35:40.795
I will assist you from here.

00:35:40.836 --> 00:35:41.962
Do you know how to do it?

00:35:43.005 --> 00:35:45.974
I... discussed the matter
with Lieutenant Torres.

00:35:46.075 --> 00:35:48.566
I think I understand the basic
principle behind her plan.

00:35:50.179 --> 00:35:52.579
How hard can it be?

00:35:52.614 --> 00:35:54.241
All right.

00:35:54.283 --> 00:35:56.251
Go to Engineering immediately.

00:35:56.285 --> 00:35:57.479
I'll contact you there.

00:36:07.930 --> 00:36:09.830
Tom, what happened?

00:36:09.865 --> 00:36:11.423
A plasma leak.

00:36:11.467 --> 00:36:12.695
Caught me in the face.

00:36:12.734 --> 00:36:13.826
Help me.

00:36:13.869 --> 00:36:15.302
Can you get to Sick Bay?

00:36:15.337 --> 00:36:16.531
The Doctor is there.

00:36:16.572 --> 00:36:17.869
Come with me.

00:36:17.906 --> 00:36:20.170
I can't,
I have to get to Engineering.

00:36:20.209 --> 00:36:22.809
You can't leave me like this.

00:36:22.942 --> 00:36:24.273
It hurts!

00:36:24.310 --> 00:36:25.937
Tom, you can walk.

00:36:26.012 --> 00:36:27.946
You have to get
to Sick Bay on your own.

00:36:28.047 --> 00:36:30.845
Kes, please.

00:36:30.883 --> 00:36:32.908
I can't.

00:36:32.952 --> 00:36:35.887
You don't want me
to get to Engineering.

00:36:35.922 --> 00:36:36.889
No.

00:36:36.923 --> 00:36:38.857
I'm... I'm hallucinating.

00:36:38.891 --> 00:36:41.621
Kes... wait!

00:36:42.728 --> 00:36:43.695
Come back!

00:36:43.729 --> 00:36:44.923
Don't leave me!

00:36:44.964 --> 00:36:46.522
Come back!

00:36:55.842 --> 00:36:57.309
Finally.

00:36:57.343 --> 00:36:58.571
What took you so long?

00:36:58.611 --> 00:37:00.636
Doctor, we have to set up
this resonance burst

00:37:00.680 --> 00:37:01.704
as quickly as possible.

00:37:01.747 --> 00:37:02.907
I've started hallucinating.

00:37:03.015 --> 00:37:06.109
Then see if Lieutenant Torres'
last program is active.

00:37:09.822 --> 00:37:11.050
I think I have it.

00:37:11.090 --> 00:37:13.058
B'Elanna was writing a program

00:37:13.092 --> 00:37:14.719
to open
a symmetrical warp field.

00:37:14.760 --> 00:37:18.025
All right.
You'll have to sequence

00:37:18.064 --> 00:37:21.033
the magnetic plasma constriction
to the following formula:

00:37:21.067 --> 00:37:25.766
T = c sub one
over theta times p sub e.

00:37:25.805 --> 00:37:27.466
How do I do that?

00:37:28.875 --> 00:37:30.103
I'm not sure.

00:37:30.142 --> 00:37:31.609
Wait a minute.

00:37:31.644 --> 00:37:33.305
I'll see if I can access

00:37:33.346 --> 00:37:35.075
Starfleet's
interactive database.

00:37:36.883 --> 00:37:38.145
Sweeting!

00:37:38.184 --> 00:37:39.583
Thank goodness I found you.

00:37:39.619 --> 00:37:41.246
Are you all right?

00:37:41.287 --> 00:37:42.584
Where have you been?

00:37:42.622 --> 00:37:43.486
In the Mess Hall

00:37:43.522 --> 00:37:45.353
trying to help
the poor souls there.

00:37:45.391 --> 00:37:47.359
Why didn't you answer
the Doctor's hails?

00:37:47.393 --> 00:37:48.451
I didn't hear them.

00:37:48.494 --> 00:37:49.961
The com system must be down,

00:37:50.062 --> 00:37:52.189
and, frankly,
I was a little busy.

00:37:52.231 --> 00:37:53.926
Ashmore thought I was a Kazon.

00:37:53.966 --> 00:37:56.230
Tried to kill me
with a carving knife.

00:37:58.137 --> 00:37:59.900
How do I know
you're really Neelix?

00:37:59.939 --> 00:38:02.499
Who else would I be?

00:38:02.541 --> 00:38:06.068
Kes, all I want to do
is protect you...

00:38:06.112 --> 00:38:07.636
to keep you safe.

00:38:07.680 --> 00:38:10.581
We have to get away from here...

00:38:10.616 --> 00:38:11.878
get to my shuttle.

00:38:16.222 --> 00:38:18.122
Doctor, have you figured out

00:38:18.157 --> 00:38:20.648
how I can enter
that sequencing code?

00:38:20.693 --> 00:38:21.785
It's quite simple really.

00:38:21.827 --> 00:38:23.624
Do you know where
the command module is?

00:38:23.663 --> 00:38:24.857
Of course.

00:38:24.897 --> 00:38:27.866
Activate it and select
"magnetic plasma sequencing."

00:38:27.900 --> 00:38:29.458
You're becoming annoying.

00:38:31.504 --> 00:38:32.801
I-I've got it.

00:38:32.838 --> 00:38:34.499
It's activated.

00:38:34.540 --> 00:38:37.304
Now it's asking me
to enter the core temperature.

00:38:37.343 --> 00:38:39.743
Move away from that console.

00:38:39.779 --> 00:38:43.772
Now, we need a temperature
high enough to emit

00:38:43.816 --> 00:38:45.613
the resonance burst,
but not so high

00:38:45.651 --> 00:38:47.380
as to irradiate
everyone on the ship.

00:38:47.420 --> 00:38:49.945
Try three million kelvins.

00:39:03.836 --> 00:39:05.701
Kes, look at him.

00:39:05.738 --> 00:39:07.899
It hurts!

00:39:07.974 --> 00:39:10.272
Look at him. Focus.

00:39:10.309 --> 00:39:11.708
I can't.

00:39:11.744 --> 00:39:13.109
Yes, you can.

00:39:13.145 --> 00:39:15.511
The mirror, remember?

00:39:15.548 --> 00:39:17.413
It hurts too much!

00:39:17.450 --> 00:39:20.647
Kes, look at him.

00:39:31.130 --> 00:39:32.495
What's the matter, Kes?

00:39:32.531 --> 00:39:33.862
Can't lift your head?

00:39:35.234 --> 00:39:36.826
Focus.

00:39:55.654 --> 00:39:57.121
Stop it!

00:40:14.607 --> 00:40:16.074
I'm all right now, Doctor,

00:40:16.108 --> 00:40:18.440
and I've entered a temperature
of three million kelvin.

00:40:18.477 --> 00:40:21.640
Then all you have to do
is activate the warp field.

00:40:21.680 --> 00:40:22.806
All right. Here we go.

00:40:38.898 --> 00:40:40.331
Kes to the Captain.

00:40:40.366 --> 00:40:42.926
If you can hear me,
please report to Engineering.

00:40:45.171 --> 00:40:46.399
What happened?

00:40:46.439 --> 00:40:47.406
It's a long story,

00:40:47.440 --> 00:40:49.340
but I think everything's
all right now.

00:40:49.375 --> 00:40:51.240
Is that who's responsible
for all this?

00:40:51.277 --> 00:40:52.335
Apparently.

00:40:52.378 --> 00:40:53.936
He looks so harmless.

00:40:53.979 --> 00:40:57.847
It's hard to believe
he almost destroyed us.

00:41:09.028 --> 00:41:11.053
You're a powerful little thing.

00:41:11.097 --> 00:41:13.895
I must say, you surprised me.

00:41:21.607 --> 00:41:23.973
Why did you do this to us?

00:41:24.043 --> 00:41:26.511
Because I can.

00:41:28.147 --> 00:41:33.517
Is it just telepathy,
or is there technology involved?

00:41:33.552 --> 00:41:35.281
Does it matter?

00:41:35.321 --> 00:41:39.280
Oh, it matters to me,
because I don't intend

00:41:39.325 --> 00:41:41.953
to let you continue
preying on others.

00:41:41.994 --> 00:41:45.088
How would you
propose to stop me?

00:41:46.966 --> 00:41:49.628
We could destroy
your technology,

00:41:49.668 --> 00:41:52.364
or adjust
your brain wave patterns

00:41:52.404 --> 00:41:54.099
to prevent telepathy,

00:41:54.140 --> 00:41:55.402
and then we could
turn you over

00:41:55.441 --> 00:41:56.999
to the government of Mithren.

00:41:57.042 --> 00:42:00.603
We could even keep you confined
in our brig

00:42:00.646 --> 00:42:02.944
behind a force field.

00:42:02.982 --> 00:42:06.418
I'm sure you're
very well-intentioned, Captain,

00:42:06.452 --> 00:42:10.081
and I'd like to be able
to accommodate you...

00:42:11.690 --> 00:42:13.487
but, you see...

00:42:13.526 --> 00:42:16.654
I'm not really here.

00:42:29.775 --> 00:42:31.538
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:42:31.577 --> 00:42:34.637
We have no explanation for
the mysterious disappearance

00:42:34.680 --> 00:42:36.739
of the telepathic alien.

00:42:36.782 --> 00:42:40.274
We can't even be certain
that he was actually here.

00:42:40.319 --> 00:42:41.752
He seems to have left us

00:42:41.787 --> 00:42:44.813
with any number
of unanswered questions.

00:42:48.827 --> 00:42:50.920
I'm surprised to see
you here, Captain.

00:42:50.963 --> 00:42:53.898
Isn't this the day
that you're usually

00:42:53.933 --> 00:42:55.730
in the holodeck with your novel?

00:42:55.768 --> 00:42:58.760
I thought
after our recent experience

00:42:58.804 --> 00:43:02.900
that I'd take a break
from fantasy for a while.

00:43:04.677 --> 00:43:05.803
I don't blame you.

00:43:05.844 --> 00:43:09.644
I think... it had quite
an impact on all of us.

00:43:14.987 --> 00:43:17.114
Do you think it's true...

00:43:17.156 --> 00:43:20.557
that the alien
was reading our minds,

00:43:20.593 --> 00:43:23.824
creating images
from our own experiences?

00:43:24.830 --> 00:43:26.559
It seemed that way.

00:43:30.536 --> 00:43:34.063
He had an uncanny ability to...

00:43:34.106 --> 00:43:37.200
bring buried thoughts
out into the open.

00:43:37.243 --> 00:43:38.835
Why?

00:43:38.877 --> 00:43:41.004
Oh, it's just...

00:43:43.015 --> 00:43:45.950
I experienced something...

00:43:45.985 --> 00:43:47.179
I'd rather not admit.

00:43:49.221 --> 00:43:50.188
I know.

00:43:50.222 --> 00:43:51.712
Me, too.

00:43:56.028 --> 00:43:57.518
But in a way...

00:43:59.832 --> 00:44:01.163
maybe he did us all a favor.

00:44:01.200 --> 00:44:02.360
Maybe it's better to...

00:44:04.536 --> 00:44:07.096
Iook those feelings in the eye

00:44:07.139 --> 00:44:10.233
than to keep them
locked up inside.

00:44:12.578 --> 00:44:14.478
I guess.

00:44:14.513 --> 00:44:16.481
I'll have to think about that.

00:44:19.818 --> 00:44:21.342
Well, I have
an early watch tomorrow,

00:44:21.387 --> 00:44:23.082
so I'd better turn in.

00:44:24.990 --> 00:44:25.957
Good night, Captain.

00:44:26.058 --> 00:44:28.686
Good night, B'Elanna.

